course: dictionary
lesson: 810
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one fits. Behave is one of these words. Read «Please behave yourself while we visit the museum.» Here behave means act in a good, polite way.
explain: The same word can mean something else in a different sentence. «Ice behaves strangely when it is heated» uses behave for how a material acts in certain conditions. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The cat behaves like a hunter at dusk» tells you behave means act or do things in a certain way. Words like good, bad, polite or strange are often clues too: «behave well», «behave badly», «behave strangely».
fact: Behave is a verb. Its forms are behave, behaves, behaved and behaving.
fact: «Behave» can mean to act or do things in a certain way, as in «behave strangely».
fact: «Behave» can mean to act in a good, polite and acceptable way, as in «behave yourself».
fact: In science, «behave» means how a material or animal acts in certain conditions: «toothpaste, ketchup and cornflour slime behave like a solid one moment and a liquid the next».
fact: «Well-behaved» means behaving well, and «badly behaved» means behaving badly.
exercise: «Please behave yourself while we visit the museum.» What does behave mean here? | Be very tired | Fall over | *Act in a good, polite way | Sing loudly
exercise: In science class, Mia writes that «cornflour slime behaves like a solid one moment and a liquid the next.» What is she describing? | A famous scientist | *How the slime acts in certain conditions | How the slime tastes | How many people made it
exercise: Which word is a form of behave? | *behaving | believe | behalf | behind
test: «Food changes how wild animals behave: bears come to food smells at a campsite.» What does behave mean here? | Grow bigger | Stay still and quiet | Be polite and kind | *Act or do things in a certain way
test: Which phrase describes a child who always acts in a good, polite way? | lost the plot | badly behaved | *well-behaved | going through a phase
exam: «Some things are tricky: ketchup behaves like a solid one moment and a liquid the next.» Which meaning of behave fits best? | Go to bed early | Act in a good, polite way | Look after yourself | *How a material acts when conditions change
